        "original_id": "12c86c32-82c5-5f5b-b220-0274233d849a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ruth Paine Home, Irving, Texas, United States\n- People: Lee Harvey Oswald, John F. Kennedy\n- Products: 6.5×52mm Carcano Model 91/38 infantry rifle, telescopic sight\n- Organizations: President's Commission on the Assassination of President Kennedy\n- Events: Assassination of John F. Kennedy\n\nFacts:\n- In March 1963, Lee Harvey Oswald used the alias \"A. Hidell\" to purchase by mail order a 6.5×52mm Carcano Model 91/38 infantry rifle with a telescopic sight.\n- The President's Commission on the Assassination of President Kennedy described the rifle purchased by Lee Harvey Oswald as a \"Mannlicher–Carcano.\"\n- On November 22, 1963, President John F. Kennedy was assassinated.\n- The Ruth Paine Home at 2515 W. 5th Street in Irving, Texas, United States, was the place where Lee Harvey Oswald spent the night before assassinating President John F. Kennedy.",
